@startuml claude-terminal-state
title One terminal tab's lifecycle (§3.1/§4.4 of claude-terminal.md)

[*] --> Spawning : "+" clicked, rfd::pick_folder() returns Some(dir)

Spawning --> Running : PtySession::spawn Ok
Spawning --> Exited : PtySession::spawn Err\n(claude not on PATH, or\ncwd failed is_dir() check) --\nerror text fed into TerminalGrid

Running --> Running : poll() drains PtyEvent::Data\ninto TerminalGrid::feed
Running --> Exited : poll() receives PtyEvent::Exited\n(reader thread hit EOF)

Exited --> [*] : close_tab (drops PtySession,\nkills child if still alive)
Running --> [*] : close_tab (drops PtySession,\nkills the running child)

note right of Exited
  Tab stays open with its final
  TerminalGrid content visible.
  Does not auto-close (§4.4).
end note

@enduml
